// Fixture: a `RepresentationWithin` bound PAIRED WITH an `: Output` occurrence.
//
// What it is for
// ──────────────
// The Mode-B (no `-o`) half of the export refusal — PRD
// `docs/prds/v0_6/precision-nominal-representation-guarantee.md`, task eta /
// C-SURFACE (2): a design that declares a `RepresentationWithin` bound the
// export path cannot demonstrate it honours must REFUSE to write the artifact
// rather than write it and report success.
//
// Before this fixture, ZERO tracked `.ri` files paired a bound with an output
// occurrence, which is exactly why the declarative Mode-B export path had never
// been exercised against a bounded module. It is consumed by
// `crates/reify-cli/tests/harness_cli/cli_representation_within.rs` and pairs
// the two halves already on main:
//   - the checker shape of `representation_within_satisfied.ri` (a structure
//     owning geometry + a separate `structure Check { param subject : X
//     constraint RepresentationWithin(subject, <bound>) }`), and
//   - the occurrence shape of `output_driver_single.ri`
//     (`sub o = STLOutput(subject: part, resolution: 0.2mm, path: "o.stl")`).
//
// The declared path is DESIGN-FILE-RELATIVE
// ─────────────────────────────────────────
// `path: "o.stl"` resolves against the *design file's* directory (io-export B7),
// NOT the cwd. A test that runs `reify build` on this file in-place would write
// `o.stl` into `tests/fixtures/`. Consumers therefore COPY this file into a
// `tempfile::tempdir()` first and run the CLI on the copy (the
// `cli_build_outputs.rs` pattern), so the artifact — or, once eta lands, its
// absence — is observed inside the tempdir.
//
// The bound value is deliberately arbitrary
// ─────────────────────────────────────────
// `1mm` here carries no measured meaning and must not be retuned against an
// achieved deviation: eta's refusal is a STATIC module-shape decision taken
// before any deviation is measured, so it fires identically for any bound,
// achievable or not. (Narrowing the refusal to genuinely unachievable bounds is
// deferred to the follow-on task tracked in the PRD's task table; it depends on
// the export path gaining a real measurement first.) Contrast
// `representation_within_satisfied.ri`, whose 1mm bound IS load-bearing and
// whose `#precision` must not be retuned casually.
//
// Geometry is deliberately CHEAP
// ──────────────────────────────
// A `box(10mm, 20mm, 5mm)` like `output_driver_single.ri`, NOT a 1 m sphere:
// the refusal fires before any measurement, so this fixture must not import the
// 5–20 s OCCT tessellation cost that the PRD §6 gate-cost rule warns about.

structure def D {
    let part = box(10mm, 20mm, 5mm)

    sub o = STLOutput(subject: part, resolution: 0.2mm, path: "o.stl")
}

// Declares the bound. `param subject : D` types the subject as
// StructureRef("D") — the same shape `SphereCheck` uses in
// `representation_within_satisfied.ri`.
structure DCheck {
    param subject : D
    constraint RepresentationWithin(subject, 1mm)
}
